# tests/startset/vmhat_walk.rxt -- [START-SET] stage 2: the VM hat's answer
# witnesses for the START-SET WALK's conservative arms (docs/design/startset.md
# §3.1, §6.3 S498-S500). A backreference, a call and a variable each read as
# "every byte, nullable" in the walk, so the pattern is not a mover; a walk
# that dropped one of those arms' bytes would make it one and the seek would
# skip the match. Every expectation is python3 re's (verify_rxt.py re-checks
# it); S498's witness is `(?1)x(y)` in vmhat.rxt, S500's (a variable) is in
# tests/vars/startset.rxt, under that directory's own oracle.

# S499: a backreference after a lookahead that captures; S would be {b} or empty
# without the A_BREF arm, and the seek would pass the a at the match start.
pattern (?=(a))\1b
features all
ms 0 "ab" 0 2
ns 1 "ab"
ns 2 "ab"
ms 0 "xab" 1 3
ms 1 "xab" 1 3
ns 2 "xab"
ns 3 "xab"
ms 0 "aab" 1 3
ms 1 "aab" 1 3
ns 2 "aab"
ns 3 "aab"
ns 0 "b"
ns 1 "b"
ms 0 "zzab" 2 4
ms 1 "zzab" 2 4
ms 2 "zzab" 2 4
ns 3 "zzab"
ns 4 "zzab"
